course: dictionary
lesson: 4690
title: Feeling homesick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Homesick is an adjective. It describes a feeling: you are away from home and you miss your home and family. «At midnight at a sleepover, Chloe gets homesick and wants to go home.» Chloe is away from home and wants to go back, so homesick means missing home.
explain: Look for clues in the sentence. The phrases «feel homesick» and «get homesick» show that it is a feeling. «A boy from Glasgow on a school camp feels homesick on the first night; he tells a teacher, and by the next afternoon, busy with canoeing, he feels much better.» Talking to a teacher and keeping busy helped him.
explain: Feeling homesick is normal, and it usually passes. «On a residential trip (one where you stay away overnight) you label your things, and feeling homesick is normal and usually passes quickly.» If you feel this way, talk to a teacher or friend, keep busy, and remember you will be home soon.
fact: Homesick is an adjective: it describes a feeling. Its comparative form is more homesick.
fact: «Homesick» means sad and missing your home and family when you are away from them.
fact: You can feel homesick on a school camp, on a sleepover, or after moving to a new country.
fact: In Chinese, «xiǎng jiā» means homesick.
fact: The American robin was named by «homesick settlers» because its red breast reminded them of home.
exercise: At midnight at a sleepover, «Chloe gets homesick and wants to go home.» What does homesick mean? | Very tired and sleepy | *Sad and missing home and family | Hungry for supper | Excited about the next day
exercise: A boy from Glasgow «feels homesick on the first night» on a school camp. What helped him feel better? | Eating nothing at all | Going to sleep alone in the car | *Telling a teacher and keeping busy with canoeing | Staying in his room and not speaking
exercise: Ali is on a school trip and misses his family every night. Which word describes how he feels? | Hometown | Careful | Hungry | *Homesick
test: On a residential trip, what should you do if you feel homesick? | Hide in your bag all day | *Tell a teacher or friend and keep busy | Pack your things and go home alone | Stop eating and sleeping
test: What does «feeling homesick is normal and usually passes quickly» tell you? | It never ends | It means you are ill | *It is a feeling that often goes away | It means you must go home at once
exam: Jayden feels homesick on his first night at camp. What should he do? | Call home every hour and cry | Lock himself in the toilet | Refuse to join in with anything | *Talk to a teacher or friend, and keep busy
